Hi Xiang,

__decode_pg_upmap_items() has a similarly bogus check based on
SIZE_MAX, prone to integer multiplication overflow -- it's basically
a cut-and-paste of __decode_pg_temp() adjusted for receiving two OSD
IDs instead of one.  I have changed __decode_pg_upmap_items() to do
len > CEPH_PG_MAX_SIZE and folded that into your patch:

https://github.com/ceph/ceph-client/commit/9f00f9cf2be293efe899db67dc5272e3a9c62717

Thanks,

